{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# Product intent\n2\t\n3\t## Purpose\n4\t\n5\tConversation Ledger preserves durable, inspectable records of visible\n6\tconversations between people and coding agents. It is a general conversation\n7\tprovenance primitive, not an intent-analysis product. Downstream consumers may\n8\tuse its records as evidence about why a repository changed, but the ledger must\n9\tnot impose that interpretation.\n10\t\n11\tThe record must remain useful to consumers beyond a single tool: cross-CLI\n12\tcontinuity, archival/export, code attribution, review, and later intent\n13\tretrieval are all valid independent uses.\n14\t\n15\t## Behavioral commitments\n16\t\n17\t- Preserve source material and provenance; do not silently rewrite history.\n18\t- Preserve exact visible turns before creating optional derived views.\n19\t- Retain enough provenance for consumers to determine applicability without\n20\t  treating any record as timeless truth.\n21\t- Record the repository, branch, commit, worktree state, author, timestamps,\n22\t  and capture mechanism with each artifact whenever available.\n23\t- Keep storage out of ordinary working-tree status views while retaining normal\n24\t  Git durability and shareability.\n25\t- Make sharing, retention, redaction, and deletion deliberate user choices.\n26\t\n27\t## Non-goals for the foundation\n28\t\n29\t- Deciding which historical statement is correct or intended.\n30\t- Summarizing, ranking, embedding, or otherwise interpreting conversations.\n31\t- Controlling an agent, enforcing a workflow, or orchestrating agents.\n32\t- Decrypting, interpreting, or reproducing reasoning the provider hides.\n33\t  Visible reasoning is recorded when exposed; reasoning withheld behind\n34\t  provider ciphertext (0.10.0+) is preserved losslessly as opaque raw state\n35\t  for a capable downstream consumer to decrypt later, but the ledger itself\n36\t  never attempts to read or reconstruct it, and stores nothing that would let\n37\t  it reproduce a native agent session on its own.\n38\t\n39\tThose belong to clients such as Turnbridge and Intent Recall, not to this core\n40\tstorage layer.\n41\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_014WAfvMiSFsFNdBMqJPkHVg","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-capture-everything","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/capture-everything","head":"1100858ed17a7ee0b377097e93eafa24d3638f68","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:9a01c126-8f0a-4060-95f9-fe3a00a2a8c3","seq":53},"id":"ev1-771cc673f39fe821a23ef26f8579c818f66229bfdd09d919bb07baccc2380ad1","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-04T03:42:36.043Z","producer":{"session_id":"9a01c126-8f0a-4060-95f9-fe3a00a2a8c3","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.221","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"main","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"1\t# Product intent\n2\t\n3\t## Purpose\n4\t\n5\tConversation Ledger preserves durable, inspectable records of visible\n6\tconversations between people and coding agents. It is a general conversation\n7\tprovenance primitive, not an intent-analysis product. Downstream consumers may\n8\tuse its records as evidence about why a repository changed, but the ledger must\n9\tnot impose that interpretation.\n10\t\n11\tThe record must remain useful to consumers beyond a single tool: cross-CLI\n12\tcontinuity, archival/export, code attribution, review, and later intent\n13\tretrieval are all valid independent uses.\n14\t\n15\t## Behavioral commitments\n16\t\n17\t- Preserve source material and provenance; do not silently rewrite history.\n18\t- Preserve exact visible turns before creating optional derived views.\n19\t- Retain enough provenance for consumers to determine applicability without\n20\t  treating any record as timeless truth.\n21\t- Record the repository, branch, commit, worktree state, author, timestamps,\n22\t  and capture mechanism with each artifact whenever available.\n23\t- Keep storage out of ordinary working-tree status views while retaining normal\n24\t  Git durability and shareability.\n25\t- Make sharing, retention, redaction, and deletion deliberate user choices.\n26\t\n27\t## Non-goals for the foundation\n28\t\n29\t- Deciding which historical statement is correct or intended.\n30\t- Summarizing, ranking, embedding, or otherwise interpreting conversations.\n31\t- Controlling an agent, enforcing a workflow, or orchestrating agents.\n32\t- Decrypting, interpreting, or reproducing reasoning the provider hides.\n33\t  Visible reasoning is recorded when exposed; reasoning withheld behind\n34\t  provider ciphertext (0.10.0+) is preserved losslessly as opaque raw state\n35\t  for a capable downstream consumer to decrypt later, but the ledger itself\n36\t  never attempts to read or reconstruct it, and stores nothing that would let\n37\t  it reproduce a native agent session on its own.\n38\t\n39\tThose belong to clients such as Turnbridge and Intent Recall, not to this core\n40\tstorage layer.\n41\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_014WAfvMiSFsFNdBMqJPkHVg","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"parentUuid":"e80b584c-c9c5-4803-95c6-698c9eb8d155","promptId":"02695425-807e-4991-87ef-01341d0e63c1","sessionId":"9a01c126-8f0a-4060-95f9-fe3a00a2a8c3","sessionKind":"bg","session_id":"9a01c126-8f0a-4060-95f9-fe3a00a2a8c3","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e80b584c-c9c5-4803-95c6-698c9eb8d155","timestamp":"2026-08-04T03:42:36.043Z","toolUseResult":{"file":{"content":"# Product intent\n\n## Purpose\n\nConversation Ledger preserves durable, inspectable records of visible\nconversations between people and coding agents. It is a general conversation\nprovenance primitive, not an intent-analysis product. Downstream consumers may\nuse its records as evidence about why a repository changed, but the ledger must\nnot impose that interpretation.\n\nThe record must remain useful to consumers beyond a single tool: cross-CLI\ncontinuity, archival/export, code attribution, review, and later intent\nretrieval are all valid independent uses.\n\n## Behavioral commitments\n\n- Preserve source material and provenance; do not silently rewrite history.\n- Preserve exact visible turns before creating optional derived views.\n- Retain enough provenance for consumers to determine applicability without\n  treating any record as timeless truth.\n- Record the repository, branch, commit, worktree state, author, timestamps,\n  and capture mechanism with each artifact whenever available.\n- Keep storage out of ordinary working-tree status views while retaining normal\n  Git durability and shareability.\n- Make sharing, retention, redaction, and deletion deliberate user choices.\n\n## Non-goals for the foundation\n\n- Deciding which historical statement is correct or intended.\n- Summarizing, ranking, embedding, or otherwise interpreting conversations.\n- Controlling an agent, enforcing a workflow, or orchestrating agents.\n- Decrypting, interpreting, or reproducing reasoning the provider hides.\n  Visible reasoning is recorded when exposed; reasoning withheld behind\n  provider ciphertext (0.10.0+) is preserved losslessly as opaque raw state\n  for a capable downstream consumer to decrypt later, but the ledger itself\n  never attempts to read or reconstruct it, and stores nothing that would let\n  it reproduce a native agent session on its own.\n\nThose belong to clients such as Turnbridge and Intent Recall, not to this core\nstorage layer.\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/docs/PRODUCT_INTENT.md","numLines":41,"startLine":1,"totalLines":41},"type":"text"},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"a8af33d6-fd15-4a53-a17b-29cc0fb2ff7c","version":"2.1.221"},"format":"claude-