{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t/**\n2\t * Format-drift handling shared by adapters. Adapters are tolerant parsers:\n3\t * a line type in neither the convertible set nor the deliberately-skipped set\n4\t * is *unrecognized* — most likely new upstream content this cledger version\n5\t * has no mapping for. Two things happen for such a line:\n6\t *\n7\t *  1. It is counted per type and surfaced in a capture-time warning (the\n8\t *     drift tripwire — \"the format changed, update cledger\").\n9\t *  2. It is preserved raw-only as an `unrecognized` event (see\n10\t *     `unrecognizedDraft`) instead of being dropped, so a later adapter\n11\t *     version can re-normalize the line rather than lose it forever.\n12\t *\n13\t * Preservation events ride the normal append path, so the capture-time\n14\t * redaction stack walks their `raw.data` exactly as it does interpreted\n15\t * events — an unrecognized line is not a hole in secret redaction.\n16\t */\n17\t\n18\timport type { EventDraft, ProducerAgentContext } from \"../schema.js\";\n19\t\n20\texport interface CaptureResult {\n21\t  appended: number;\n22\t  deduped: number;\n23\t  /** Skipped-line tallies keyed by unrecognized type, e.g. {\"response_item/agent_message\": 3}. */\n24\t  unrecognized: Record<string, number>;\n25\t}\n26\t\n27\texport function countUnrecognized(unrecognized: Record<string, number>, key: string): void {\n28\t  unrecognized[key] = (unrecognized[key] ?? 0) + 1;\n29\t}\n30\t\n31\t/**\n32\t * Build the raw-only preservation event for one unrecognized transcript line.\n33\t *\n34\t * `content` holds only the type label — the ledger did not interpret the\n35\t * line, so it claims no roles, no actor identity (actor is `system`), no\n36\t * structured blocks. The full source line lives under `raw.data`, versioned\n37\t * by `rawFormat` so a future adapter knows which native shape to re-parse.\n38\t *\n39\t * Identity