{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_0166AQpMpQLHjwvpidAwmVFP","input":{"command":"git reset -q --soft HEAD~1 && git add -A && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nCapture the whole record, not just the turns\n\nEvery adapter kept a list of transcript line types it parsed and threw away\nas \"session bookkeeping, UI state, and file-history machinery\". That list was\nthe largest remaining source of loss at capture, and most of what it dropped\nis exactly what a downstream consumer needs: whether an agent was sandboxed\nwhen it said something, what a file looked like between two commits, what a\nsubagent actually did to produce its one-line answer.\n\nFour new kinds, and a rule for which is which:\n\n  session_state      a declaration that holds until restated — mode,\n                     permission mode, sandbox/approval policy, model\n                     settings, title, worktree relocation, codex\n                     turn_context/session_meta/world_state\n  activity           a point-in-time occurrence that is not a turn — hooks,\n                     turn durations, token counts, task lifecycle, queue\n                     operations, compaction, opencode step boundaries\n  context_injection  material the harness put into the model's context that\n                     nobody typed — Claude Code attachment lines\n  file_snapshot      intermediate file state between commits\n\nAll four use one content shape: a *_type discriminator naming the source's\nown type verbatim, the source's own field names beside it, and `blocks` in\nthe ordinary [{type,text}] form wherever a record carries prose, so text\nextraction needs no per-kind special case.\n\nThe skip lists are gone, except for codex's two event_msg payload types that\ngenuinely duplicate a response_item. Keeping a skip list required a type to\nbe both known and worthless, and almost nothing was. Removing a type from a\nskip list would previously route it to the *unrecognized* branch — preserved,\nbut drift-warned, which is wrong for a known upstream type and would have\nmade the drift warning stop meaning \"the format moved\". Now the routing has a\nthird destination instead.\n\nTwo structural additions make it work:\n\nConversationRef.parent makes a sub-conversation expressible. Claude Code\nsidechains and opencode subagent sessions were both dropped entirely; each is\nnow its own conversation pointing back at the session that spawned it, so\n`show <subagent>` reads one in isolation and `show <session>` still matches\nthe whole tree. opencode child sessions are only reachable via the parent's\n`task` tool part metadata (`session list` returns top-level sessions only),\nso capture walks them depth-first, cycle-guarded.\n\nEvidenceEvent.resolved holds what the ledger read at capture time from\npointers the source only names — today, the sha256 and size of a Claude Code\nfile-history backup. It is deliberately outside the identity subset: the\nbacking cache is machine-local and prunable, so the same line resolves\ndifferently elsewhere, and folding it into the id would duplicate every\nsnapshot on a rescan after a prune. Digests, not bytes: the redaction stack\nwalks content and raw.data, not this field.\n\nDisplay is separate from capture. log/show/conversations hide the four new\nkinds behind --with-state, because a session restates its mode and tracked\nfiles far more often than anyone speaks. Capture, export and sync are\nunaffected.\n\nExisting ledgers upgrade: `cledger renormalize` now reconstructs non-turn\nrecords from lines preserved as `unrecognized` before the adapters knew them,\nwith the same id a live capture produces, so the two dedup. file_snapshot is\nexcluded from that path on purpose — the cache its pointers name is long gone\nby the time anyone runs renormalize, and an upgrade would permanently displace\na preserved line with a digest-less record.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011yyjMrYMdcPPiKnPmUm8Hs\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2","description":"Commit the work"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-capture-everything","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/capture-everything","head":"1100858ed17a7ee0b377097e93eafa24d3638f68","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:9a01c126-8f0a-4060-95f9-fe3a00a2a8c3","seq":665},"id":"ev1-a12ead810775c611e5e4810e8da75f4c52458d91b0f5cc3ce28553ddfb42fee8","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-04T04:13:09.516Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"9a01c126-8f0a-4060-95f9-fe3a00a2a8c3","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.221","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/capture-everything","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-capture-everything","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_0166AQpMpQLHjwvpidAwmVFP","input":{"command":"git reset -q --soft HEAD~1 && git add -A && git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nCapture the whole record, not just the turns\n\nEvery adapter kept a list of transcript line types it parsed and threw away\nas \"session bookkeeping, UI state, and file-history machinery\". That list was\nthe largest remaining source of loss at capture, and most of what it dropped\nis exactly what a downstream consumer needs: whether an agent was sandboxed\nwhen it said something, what a file looked like between two commits, what a\nsubagent actually did to produce its one-line answer.\n\nFour new kinds, and a rule for which is which:\n\n  session_state      a declaration that holds until restated — mode,\n                     permission mode, sandbox/approval policy, mo