{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_0166SnzkQi55QpcEzEaUvwsJ","input":{"content":"---\nname: project-cledger-full-capture\ndescription: 0.19.0 (PR #4) removed the per-adapter skip lists; four new record kinds, ConversationRef.parent, EvidenceEvent.resolved, and what was deliberately left out\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nShipped 2026-08-04 as 0.19.0 on branch `worktree-capture-everything`, PR #4 (draft, based on the two then-unpushed local `main` commits 6616d12/44bc186, which ride along in the diff).\n\n**What changed.** The `KNOWN_SKIPPED_LINE_TYPES` / `KNOWN_SKIPPED_PART_TYPES` lists are gone from all three adapters. Four new kinds in `KNOWN_KINDS`: `session_state` (declaration holding until restated), `activity` (point-in-time occurrence that is not a turn), `context_injection` (harness-inserted context material), `file_snapshot` (intermediate file state). Builders live in `src/adapters/records.ts`, the counterpart to `drift.ts`. One content shape everywhere: `*_type` discriminator (spread *last*, so a source field cannot clobber it) + source field names verbatim + `blocks` for prose.\n\n**Decisions worth remembering:**\n\n- The only surviving skip is codex `event_msg` payload types `agent_message`/`user_message` — genuine duplicates of a `response_item`. Everything else in `event_msg` (token counts, task lifecycle, sub-agent activity, aborts) has no twin and is `activity`.\n- Claude Code `system` lines split on **whether `content` is a non-empty string**, not on a subtype list: text means the user read it, so it is a `conversation_turn` with actor `system`. A subtype list would go stale.\n- `EvidenceEvent.resolved` is a new top-level field, **outside the identity subset**, holding capture-time resolution of machine-local pointers (today: sha256 + bytes of a Claude Code file-history backup). Digests only, never file bodies — the redaction stack walks `content`/`raw.data`, not this.\n- `ConversationRef.parent` is **inside** identity. Claude sidechains become `claude-code:<session>#agent:<agentId>`; opencode subagent sessions keep their own id and gain a parent.\n- opencode child sessions are discoverable *only* via the parent's `task` tool part `state.metadata.sessionId` — `opencode session list` returns top-level sessions only. Capture recurses depth-first with a `visited` guard.\n- Claude Code stores subagents two ways depending on version: inline `isSidechain` lines, and separate `<session>/subagents/agent-*.jsonl` files. `fileHistoryDir` therefore walks up to the `projects` directory instead of counting `dirname` calls.\n- `renormalize` upgrades previously-`unrecognized` non-turn lines into their record kind with id fidelity (tested), but **deliberately excludes `file_snapshot`** — the backup cache is long pruned by then, so the upgrade would displace a resolvable line with a digest-less record.\n- Display is separate from capture: `SESSION_MACHINERY_KINDS` are hidden from `log`/`show`/`conversations` behind `--with-state`. Sources restate mode/tracked-files far more often than anyone speaks.\n\n**Left open (now in the README roadmap):** capturing file *content* rather than just digests (wants a size policy + opt-in); codex `agent_message` embedded `encrypted_content` blocks still dropped rather than sealed; whether codex writes separate rollouts for sub-agents is unconfirmed, so codex sub-agent internals may still be unrecorded.\n\nRelated: [[project-cledger-opencode-adapter]], [[project-cledger-reasoning-preservation]], [[project-ledger-ecosystem]].\n","file_path":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/memory/project-cledger-full-capture.md"},"name":"Write","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-capture-everything","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/capture-everything","head":"1100858ed17a7ee0b377097e93eafa24d3