{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01JwBcsT1hYG9LiLihKcFN98","input":{"command":"gh pr create --draft --base main --title \"Capture the whole record, not just the turns\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nRemoves the per-adapter \"known skipped line types\" lists and gives the types they discarded real structure. This is the change the `KNOWN_SKIPPED_LINE_TYPES` roadmap entry asked for, extended across all three CLIs.\n\n## What was being lost\n\nEach adapter parsed a set of line types and threw them away as bookkeeping. Measured over ~200 recent local sessions, that was roughly **a third of every Claude Code transcript** and **half of every codex rollout** — including the only records of intermediate file state, of the sandbox and approval policy a turn ran under, and of every subagent's internal work.\n\n## Four new kinds\n\n| Kind | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `session_state` | A declaration that holds until restated — mode, permission mode, sandbox/approval policy, model settings, title, worktree relocation, codex `turn_context`/`session_meta`/`world_state` |\n| `activity` | A point-in-time occurrence that is not a turn — hooks, turn durations, token counts, task lifecycle, queue operations, compaction, opencode step boundaries |\n| `context_injection` | Material the harness put into the model's context that nobody typed — Claude Code `attachment` lines |\n| `file_snapshot` | Intermediate file state: the versions a file passed through between commits |\n\nOne content shape across all four: a `*_type` discriminator naming the source's own type verbatim, the source's own field names beside it, and `blocks` in the ordinary `[{type,text}]` form wherever a record carries prose — so text extraction needs no per-kind special case.\n\nThe skip lists are gone, except codex's two `event_msg` payload types that genuinely duplicate a `response_item`. A skip list required a type to be both *known* and *worthless*, and almost nothing was.\n\n## Sub-conversations\n\n`ConversationRef.parent` makes the parent/child relation expressible, which is what was blocking subagent capture. Claude Code sidechains and opencode subagent sessions were both dropped entirely; each is now its own conversation pointing back at its parent, so `show <subagent>` reads one in isolation and `show <session>` still matches the whole tree.\n\nopencode child sessions are reachable *only* through the parent's `task` tool part metadata — `opencode session list` returns top-level sessions only — so capture walks them depth-first, cycle-guarded.\n\n## `EvidenceEvent.resolved`\n\nFile-history lines carry pointers into a machine-local cache, never content. Capture records the pointer in `content` and the sha256 + size it read in a new top-level `resolved` field, kept **outside the identity subset** on purpose: the cache is prunable, so the same line resolves differently elsewhere, and folding it into the id would duplicate every snapshot on a rescan after a prune. Digests, not bytes — the redaction stack walks `content` and `raw.data`, not this field.\n\n## Display\n\n`log`/`show`/`conversations` hide the four new kinds behind `--with-state`. A session restates its mode and tracked files far more often than anyone speaks. Capture, export and sync are unaffected.\n\n## Upgrade path\n\n`cledger renormalize` now reconstructs non-turn records from lines preserved as `unrecognized` before the adapters knew them, with the exact id a live capture produces so the two dedup (there's a test asserting this). `file_snapshot` is excluded on purpose — the cache its pointers name is long gone by then, and the upgrade would permanently displace a preserved line with a digest-less record.\n\n## Verification\n\n- 176 tests pass, including new coverage for each mapping, the file-digest resolution (present *and* missing backup), the codex `event_msg` split, subagent conversations, and renormalize id-fidelity for non-turn records.\n- Smoke-tested end to end against real local transcripts from all three CLIs: 653 turns / 326 activity / 84 session_state / 14 file_snapshot / 12 context_injection / 210 reasoning, backup digests resolving, `cledger scan` clean.\n\n## Roadmap\n\nRetires the `KNOWN_SKIPPED_LINE_TYPES` and \"subagent sessions are dropped\" entries; adds three honest successors — capturing file *content* rather than just digests, codex `agent_message` encrypted blocks still being dropped, and unconfirmed codex sub-agent rollout coverage.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_011yyjMrYMdcPPiKnPmUm8Hs\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Open draft PR"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-capture-everything","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/capture-everything","head":"1100858ed17a7ee0b377097e93eafa24d3638f68","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:9a01c126-8f0a-4060-95f9-fe3a00a2a8c3","seq":677},"id":"ev1-668668efd75ddcc1cad01a9f776866ea647a2f4f25a47b381d7f1a6b55f73bf0","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-04T04:13:41.412Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"9a01c126-8f0a-4060-95f9-fe3a00a2a8c3","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.221","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/capture-everything","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-capture-everything","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01JwBcsT1hYG9LiLihKcFN98","input":{"command":"gh pr create --draft --base main --title \"Capture the whole record, not just the turns\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nRemoves the per-adapter \"known skipped line types\" lists and gives the types they discarded real structure. This is the change the `KNO