{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Done. Draft PR #4 is open: **https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/4**\n\n**Sanity check before finishing:** 176 tests pass, 0 failures; `npx tsc --noEmit` clean; working tree clean; and I smoke-tested all three adapters against real local transcripts in a scratch repo — 653 turns / 326 activity / 84 session_state / 14 file_snapshot / 12 context_injection / 210 reasoning, with backup digests actually resolving and `cledger scan` reporting no findings.\n\n**What I found first.** I sampled ~200 local Claude Code transcripts, 60 codex rollouts, and an opencode export to see what the skip lists were actually discarding. It was roughly a third of every Claude transcript and half of every codex rollout — and it included types nobody had catalogued (`agent-setting`, `worktree-state`, `pr-link`, `bridge-session`, `relocated`), which were silently tripping the drift warning.\n\n**What I built.** Four new kinds, split on a rule rather than per-source taste: `session_state` (a declaration holding until restated), `activity` (an occurrence that isn't a turn), `context_injection` (context the harness inserted that nobody typed), `file_snapshot` (file versions between commits). One content shape for all of them — the source's own type name as a discriminator, the source's own field names beside it, and `blocks` wherever there's prose so text extraction never needs a per-kind case.\n\nThe skip lists are gone except for codex's two `event_msg` payload types that genuinely duplicate a `response_item`. Your roadmap note anticipated the trap — removing a type from the skip set routes it to the *unrecognized* branch, which is semantically wrong for a known type — so the routing gained a third destination instead of a wider drift funnel.\n\nTwo things I did beyond the literal ask, because \"record everything\" made them hard to leave: `ConversationRef.parent` (Claude sidechains and opencode subagent sessions were being dropped entirely — for opencode, children are only reachable through the parent's `task` tool metadata, so capture now walks them), and `EvidenceEvent.resolved` for the file-history digests. `resolved` sits *outside* event identity deliberately: the backup cache is prunable, so folding a digest into the id would duplicate every snapshot on a rescan after a cleanup.\n\n**Two things worth your attention.** The PR is based on your two unpushed local `main` commits, so they appear in its diff. And I retired both the `KNOWN_SKIPPED_LINE_TYPES` and \"subagent sessions are dropped\" roadmap entries, replacing them with three honest successors — capturing file *content* rather than digests, codex `agent_message` encrypted blocks still being dropped, and unconfirmed codex sub-agent rollout coverage.\n\nresult: conversation-ledger 0.19.0 removes the skip lists across all three CLI adapters — four new record kinds, sub-conversation capture, and capture-time file digests — shipped as draft PR #4 with 176 tests passing.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"worktree-capture-everything","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/capture-everything","head":"1100858ed17a7ee0b377097e93eafa24d3638f68","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"conversation":{"id":"claude-code:9a01c126-8f0a-4060-95f9-fe3a00a2a8c3","seq":698},"id":"ev1-e0e243292858d45934656d50a67c97781a8fe596f0a969975c94bfe4bbe4cff8","kind":"conversation_turn","occurred_at":"2026-08-04T04:15:05.862Z","producer":{"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"9a01c126-8f0a-4060-95f9-fe3a00a2a8c3","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.221","tool":"cledger","version":"0.18.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger/.claude/worktrees/capture-everything","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"worktree-capture-everything","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"Don